						<h3 id="n2" class="imgTitle"><img src="images/h2_2.gif" width="274" height="25" alt="b. Establishment of the Imperial Diet" /></h3>
						<div class="col1">
							<p class="text">The impending establishment of the Diet, saw the Daido Danketsu (Grand Coalition) Movement surge with the aim of uniting the elements of the People's Rights Movement; eventually, it led to the formation of the Constitutional Liberal Party (Rikken Jiyuto), with members of the former Liberal Party at its core. When the Imperial Diet was inaugurated in 1890 (Meiji 23), the Government, led by the Satsuma-Choshu clique, adopted the so-called &quot;transcendental&quot; (chozen-shugi) policy of keeping distance from all political parties. That stance led to fierce confrontation between the Government and the popular parties in the first session of the Diet.</p>
						</div>
